# ziptastic — CHCE Native Engine — Agent Build Instructions

You are building **ziptastic**, the native engine of CHCE (Chimera Hybrid
Compression Engine). Read this entire document before writing any code.
Every phase must pass its tests before the next phase begins.

---

## 1. Mission

Build a single-binary, offline, closed-source-safe compression engine that:

1. Beats `xz -9` by **≥3%** on Deflate-heavy archives (ZIP, PDF, PNG, nightly builds).
2. Is **never worse than `xz -9`** by more than 0.5% on any input (hard guarantee via LZMA2 fallback).
3. With `--max-ratio`, approaches the `paq8px` ratio class on general data.

The engine composes preprocessors (SREP, Preflate), a dual-resolution match
finder, a joint parser, and per-block entropy backends (rANS, Huffman, LZMA2
fallback, and an optional CM bridge) into a **single unified format**. It does
not shell out to external binaries.

---

## 2. Hard Constraints

- **Offline only.** No network calls, no model downloads, no GPU.
- **No external processes.** Everything is linked or compiled in.
- **Codecs live under `vendor/hcs/old/<id>/`.** Read them, link them, or
  copy their C sources into `src/codecs/<id>/`. Do not modify `vendor/hcs/`
  in place — treat it as read-only. Any change must be a wrapper in `src/`.
- **CMake only.** No other build system.
- **C++20** for new engine code. C is fine for vendored source copies.
- **License-safe.** Never link `paq8px`, `upx`, `advancecomp`, `packJPG`, or
  `lzo` (GPL/LGPL). They are external-process-only in `heavenzip`.
  Everything in `src/` must remain linkable into a closed-source binary.

