## 9. Acceptance Criteria (Whole Project)

- `ziptastic -9 corpus/` produces `≤ xz -9 corpus/` on the entire Silesia corpus.
- `ziptastic -9 silesia.zip` produces `≤ 44.0 MiB` (beats `xz -9` by ≥3%).
- `ziptastic --max-ratio silesia/` produces `≤ 42 MiB` (approaches ZPAQ class).
- Decompression speed on default mode ≥ 100 MB/s on modern hardware.
- Zero network calls, zero external processes, zero model files.
- Builds cleanly on Linux, macOS, Windows with only CMake + a C++20 compiler.

